<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="RUT" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Ruth</para>
  <para style="mt">Ruth</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass in the days when the ruled, that there was a famine in the land. And a certain man of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah went to sojourn in the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, he, and his wife, and his two sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the name of the man <char style="add">[was]</char> Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char>, and the name of his wife Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, and the name of his two sons Machlon <char style="add">[sick]</char> and Kilyon <char style="add">[pining]</char>, Efratim <char style="add">[ashiness: fruitfulness]</char> from Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in Y’hudah. And they came into the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and settled there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char> Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>’s husband died; and she was left, and her two sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they took them wives of the women of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>; the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Orpah <char style="add">[gazelle]</char>, and the name of the other Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char>: and they dwelled there about ten years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Machlon <char style="add">[sick]</char> and Kilyon <char style="add">[pining]</char> died also both of them; and the woman was left of her two sons and her husband.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then she arose with her daughters in law, that she might return from the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: for she had heard in the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> how that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had visited his people in giving them bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For what reason she went forth out of the place where she was, and her two daughters in law with her; and they went on the way to return unto the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> said unto her two daughters in law, Go, return each to her mother’s house: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> deal kindly with you, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have dealt with the dead, and with me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> grant you that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may find rest, each <char style="add">[of you]</char> in the house of her husband. Then she kissed them; and they lifted up their voice, and wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they said unto her, Surely we will return with you<char style="ord">i</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> said, Turn again, my daughters: why will you<char style="ord">2f</char> go with me? <char style="add">[are]</char> there yet <char style="add">[any more]</char> sons in my womb, that they may be your husbands?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Turn again, my daughters, go <char style="add">[your way]</char>; for I am too old to have an husband. If I should say, I have hope, <char style="add">[if]</char> I should have an husband also to night, and should also bear sons;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Would you<char style="ord">2f</char> wait for them till they were grown? would you<char style="ord">2f</char> stay for them from having husbands? No, my daughters; for it grieves me much for your sakes that the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is gone out against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they lifted up their voice, and wept again: and ‘Orpah <char style="add">[gazelle]</char> kissed her mother in law; but Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> clave unto her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And she said, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> sister in law is gone back unto her people, and unto her gods: return you<char style="ord">i</char> after you<char style="ord">i</char> sister in law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> said, Intreat me not to leave you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[or]</char> to return from following after you<char style="ord">i</char>: for to which you<char style="ord">i</char> go, I will go; and where you<char style="ord">i</char> lodge, I will lodge: your<char style="ord">i</char> people <char style="add">[shall be]</char> my people, and your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Where you<char style="ord">i</char> die, will I die, and there will I be buried: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> do so to me, and more also, <char style="add">[if ought]</char> but death part you<char style="ord">i</char> and me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />When she saw that she was steadfastly minded to go with her, then she left speaking unto her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So they two went until they came to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>. And it came to pass, when they were come to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>, that all the city was moved about them, and they said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> this Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And she said unto them, Call me not Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, call me Mara: for the Almighty has dealt very bitterly with me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />I went out full, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has brought me home again empty: why <char style="add">[then]</char> call you<char style="ord">2f</char> me Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, seeing the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has testified against me, and the Almighty <char style="pn">(Shaddai)</char> has afflicted me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> returned, and Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> the Moavi <char style="add">[from father: what father?]</char>, her daughter in law, with her, which returned out of the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: and they came to Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> in the beginning of barley harvest.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> had a kinsman of her husband’s, a mighty man of wealth, of the family of Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char>; and his name <char style="add">[was]</char> Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> the Moaviah [from father: what father?] said unto Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, Let me now go to the field, and glean ears of corn after <char style="add">[him]</char> in whose sight I shall find grace. And she said unto her, Go, my daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And she went, and came, and gleaned in the field after the reapers: and she happened to light on a part of the field <char style="add">[belonging]</char> unto Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> of the family of Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And, behold, Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> came from Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>, and said unto the reapers, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> with you. And they answered him, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> bless you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then said Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> unto his servant that was set over the reapers, Whose girl <char style="add">[is]</char> this?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the servant that was set over the reapers answered and said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> the Moavi [from father: what father?] girl that came back with Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> out of the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And she said, I pray you, let me glean and gather after the reapers among the sheaves: so she came, and has continued even from the morning until now, that she tarried a little in the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> unto Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char>, Hear you<char style="ord">i</char> not, my daughter? Go not to glean in another field, neither go from hence, but abide here fast by my maidens:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Let]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes <char style="add">[be]</char> on the field that they do reap, and go you<char style="ord">i</char> after them: have I not charged the young men that they shall not touch you<char style="ord">i</char>? and when you<char style="ord">i</char> are athirst, go unto the vessels, and drink of <char style="add">[that]</char> which the young men have drawn.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then she fell on her face, and bowed herself to the ground, and said unto him, Why have I found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should take knowledge of me, seeing I <char style="add">[am]</char> a stranger?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> answered and said unto her, It has fully been showed me, all that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done unto you<char style="ord">i</char> mother in law since the death of you<char style="ord">i</char> husband: and <char style="add">[how]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have left you<char style="ord">i</char> father and you<char style="ord">i</char> mother, and the land of you<char style="ord">i</char> nativity, and are come unto a people which you<char style="ord">i</char> knew not heretofore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> recompense you<char style="ord">i</char> work, and a full reward be given you<char style="ord">i</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, under whose wings you<char style="ord">i</char> are come to trust.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then she said, Let me find favour in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight, my lord; for that you<char style="ord">i</char> have comforted me, and for that you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken friendly unto you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, though I be not like unto one of your<char style="ord">i</char> handmaidens.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> said unto her, At mealtime come you<char style="ord">i</char> here, and eat of the bread, and dip you<char style="ord">i</char> morsel in the vinegar. And she sat beside the reapers: and he reached her parched <char style="add">[corn]</char>, and she did eat, and was sufficed, and left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when she was risen up to glean, Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> commanded his young men, saying, Let her glean even among the sheaves, and reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> her not:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And let fall also <char style="add">[some]</char> of the handfuls of purpose for her, and leave <char style="add">[them]</char>, that she may glean <char style="add">[them]</char>, and rebuke <char style="pn">(reprimand; strongly warn; restrain)</char> her not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />So she gleaned in the field until even, and beat out that she had gleaned: and it was about an eifah of barley.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And she took <char style="add">[it]</char> up, and went into the city: and her mother in law saw what she had gleaned: and she brought forth, and gave to her that she had reserved after she was sufficed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And her mother in law said unto her, Where have you<char style="ord">i</char> gleaned to day? and where worked you<char style="ord">i</char>? Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> be he that did take knowledge of you<char style="ord">i</char>. And she showed her mother in law with whom she had wrought, and said, The man’s name with whom I wrought to day <char style="add">[is]</char> Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> said unto her daughter in law, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> he of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who has not left off his kindness to the living and to the dead. And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> said unto her, The man <char style="add">[is]</char> near of family unto us, one of our next kinsmen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> the Moavi <char style="add">[from father: what father?]</char> said, He said unto me also, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall keep fast by my young men, until they have ended all my harvest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> said unto Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> her daughter in law, <char style="add">[It is]</char> good, my daughter, that you<char style="ord">i</char> go out with his maidens, that they meet you<char style="ord">i</char> not in any other field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So she kept fast by the maidens of Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> to glean unto the end of barley harvest and of wheat harvest; and dwelt with her mother in law.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> her mother in law said unto her, My daughter, shall I not seek rest for you<char style="ord">i</char>, that it may be well with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And now <char style="add">[is]</char> not Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> of our family, with whose maidens you<char style="ord">i</char> were? Behold, he removes <char style="pn">(chaff)</char> from barley to night in the threshing floor.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Wash yourself therefore, and anoint you<char style="ord">i</char>, and put your<char style="ord">i</char> clothing upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and get you<char style="ord">i</char> down to the floor: <char style="add">[but]</char> make not yourself known unto the man, until he shall have done eating and drinking.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it shall be, when he lies down, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall mark the place where he shall lie, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go in, and uncover his feet, and lay you<char style="ord">i</char> down; and he will tell you<char style="ord">i</char> what you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And she said unto her, All that you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto me I will do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And she went down unto the floor, and did according to all that her mother in law bade her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> had eaten and drunk, and his heart was merry, he went to lie down at the end of the heap of corn: and she came softly, and uncovered his feet, and laid her down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it came to pass at midnight, that the man was afraid, and turned himself: and, behold, a woman lay at his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said, Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? And she answered, I <char style="add">[am]</char> Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant: spread therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> skirt over you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a near kinsman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, my daughter: <char style="add">[for]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have showed more kindness in the latter end than at the beginning, inasmuch as you<char style="ord">i</char> followed not young men, whether poor or rich.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And now, my daughter, fear not; I will do to you<char style="ord">i</char> all that you<char style="ord">i</char> require: for all the city of my people does know that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a virtuous woman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And now it is true that I <char style="add">[am your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> near kinsman: howbeit there is a kinsman nearer than I.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Tarry this night, and it shall be in the morning, <char style="add">[that]</char> if he will perform unto you<char style="ord">i</char> the part of a kinsman, well; let him do the kinsman’s part: but if he will not do the part of a kinsman to you<char style="ord">i</char>, then will I do the part of a kinsman to you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives: lie down until the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And she lay at his feet until the morning: and she rose up before one could know another. And he said, Let it not be known that a woman came into the floor.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Also he said, Bring the veil that <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> have]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and hold it. And when she held it, he measured six <char style="add">[measures]</char> of barley, and laid <char style="add">[it]</char> on her: and she went into the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when she came to her mother in law, she said, Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, my daughter? And she told her all that the man had done to her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And she said, These six <char style="add">[measures]</char> of barley gave he me; for he said to me, Go not empty unto you<char style="ord">i</char> mother in law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then said she, Sit still, my daughter, until you<char style="ord">i</char> know how the matter will fall: for the man will not be in rest, until he have finished the thing this day.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then went Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> up to the gate, and sat him down there: and, behold, the kinsman of whom Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> spoke came by; unto whom he said, Ho, such a one! turn aside, sit down here. And he turned aside, and sat down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he took ten men of the elders of the city, and said, Sit you<char style="ord">2f</char> down here. And they sat down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he said unto the kinsman, Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, that is come again out of the country of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, sells a parcel of land, which <char style="add">[was]</char> our brother Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char>’s:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And I thought to advertise <char style="pn">(to advise, warn, inform, reveal)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Buy <char style="add">[it]</char> before the inhabitants, and before the elders of my people. If you<char style="ord">i</char> will redeem <char style="add">[it]</char>, redeem <char style="add">[it]</char>: but if you<char style="ord">i</char> will not redeem <char style="add">[it, then]</char> tell me, that I may know: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> none to redeem <char style="add">[it]</char> beside you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I <char style="add">[am]</char> after you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he said, I will redeem <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then said Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>, What day you<char style="ord">i</char> buy the field of the hand of Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> must buy <char style="add">[it]</char> also of Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> the Moaviah [from father: what father?], the wife of the dead, to raise up the name of the dead upon his inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the kinsman said, I cannot redeem <char style="add">[it]</char> for myself, lest I mar my own inheritance: redeem you<char style="ord">i</char> my right to yourself; for I cannot redeem <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now this <char style="add">[was the manner]</char> in former time in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> concerning redeeming and concerning changing, for to confirm all things; a man plucked off his shoe, and gave <char style="add">[it]</char> to his neighbour: and this <char style="add">[was]</char> a testimony in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore the kinsman said unto Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>, Buy <char style="add">[it]</char> for you<char style="ord">i</char>. So he drew off his shoe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> said unto the elders, and <char style="add">[unto]</char> all the people, You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> witnesses this day, that I have bought all that <char style="add">[was]</char> Eli-Melekh <char style="add">[my God is king]</char>’s, and all that <char style="add">[was]</char> Kilyon’s <char style="add">[pining]</char>’s and Machlon’s <char style="add">[sick]</char>’s, of the hand of Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Moreover Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char> the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, the wife of Machlon <char style="add">[sick]</char>, have I purchased to be my wife, to raise up the name of the dead upon his inheritance, that the name of the dead be not cut off from among his brethren, and from the gate of his place: you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> witnesses this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the gate, and the elders, said, <char style="add">[We are]</char> witnesses. The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> make the woman that is come into you<char style="ord">i</char> house like Rachel and like Leah, which two did build the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and do you<char style="ord">i</char> worthily in Ephrat <char style="add">[ash-heap: place of fruitfulness]</char>, and be famous in Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And let you<char style="ord">i</char> house be like the house of Partzi <char style="add">[Breach (breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)]</char>, whom Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> bore unto Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, of the seed which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall give you<char style="ord">i</char> of this young woman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> took Rut <char style="add">[friendship]</char>, and she was his wife: and when he went in unto her, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave her conception, and she bore a son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the women said unto Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which has not left you<char style="ord">i</char> this day without a kinsman, that his name may be famous in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he shall be unto you<char style="ord">i</char> a restorer of <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> life, and a nourisher of you<char style="ord">i</char> old age: for you<char style="ord">i</char> daughter in law, which loves you<char style="ord">i</char>, which is better to you<char style="ord">i</char> than seven sons, has born him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char> took the child, and laid it in her bosom, and became nurse unto it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the women her neighbours gave it a name, saying, There is a son born to Na’omi <char style="add">[my delight]</char>; and they called his name ‘Oved <char style="add">[serving]</char>: he <char style="add">[is]</char> the father of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, the father of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the generations of Partzi <char style="add">[Breach (breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)]</char>: Partzi [Breach (breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)] begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Hetzron <char style="add">[surrounded by a wall]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Hetzron <char style="add">[surrounded by a wall]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Ram <char style="add">[high or exalted]</char>, and Ram <char style="add">[high or exalted]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> ‘Amminadav <char style="add">[family of the prince]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And ‘Amminadav <char style="add">[family of the prince]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Nachshon <char style="add">[Enchanter]</char>, and Nachshon <char style="add">[Enchanter]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Salmon,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Salmon begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>, and Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> ‘Oved <char style="add">[serving]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And ‘Oved <char style="add">[serving]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>, and Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
</usx>